      "writtenOn": "2017-02-08T19:26:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u0027candidate\u0027 is the WifiConfiguration of the recommended network. targetBssid is initially assigned from the BSSID field of the ScanResult which leads to the recommendation of this network. So it cannot start as null or ANY. We then overwrite this targetBssid variable to ANY only if firmware supports roaming and app didn\u0027t specify a particular BSSID for connection to this network (i.e. the BSSID field of this WifiConfiguration is either null or ANY).\n\nRegarding whether to give a BSSID to start with, I think it is better not to. Given we don\u0027t control the firmware behavior, the starting BSSID we choose may not match what firmware picks. That would cause an extra firmware roaming. Why not just let firmware decide which one to connect to?",
      "parentUuid": "813a23fd_e2b03538",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 637,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 638,
        "endChar": 90
      },
